{"text": "creation", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">creacion</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">creacioun</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">creation</i>, from Old French <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fro\">creacion</i> (French <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fr\">cr\u00e9ation</i>), from Latin <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">cre\u0101ti\u014d, cre\u0101ti\u014dnis</i>; equivalent to <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">create</i> +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">-ion</i>. Displaced native Old English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ang\">\u0121es\u010beaft</i>.\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "(countable) Something created such as an invention or artwork.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "(uncountable) The act of creating something.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "(uncountable) All which exists.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["Received Pronunciation", "/k\u0279i\u02c8e\u026a\u0283\u0259n/"], ["IPA", "[k\u0279i\u02c8\u02b2e\u026a\u0283\u0258n]"]]}